<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-1225] Errors before the last shell command are ignored </title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-1225</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;If run the following command in shell interpreter. It just run normally without any error message. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;hello
pwd
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The root cause is that command &quot;bash -c &amp;lt;shell scripts&amp;gt;&quot; will always return 0 as long as the last line of shell script run correctly. &lt;/p&gt;</description>
