	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;
		&lt;ol&gt;
			&lt;li&gt;What is this PR for?&lt;br/&gt;
    The problem is that command &quot;bash -c &amp;lt;shell scripts&amp;gt;&quot; will always return 0 as long as the last line of shell script run correctly. e.g the following command will run correctly without any error message.&lt;br/&gt;
    ```&lt;br/&gt;
    hello&lt;br/&gt;
    pwd&lt;br/&gt;
    ``` &lt;br/&gt;
    This PR will redirect stderr and stdout to the same place, and will display both the stderr and stdout to frontend just like what user see in the native shell terminal. So the output of above command will be as following&lt;br/&gt;
    ```&lt;br/&gt;
    bash: hello: command not found&lt;br/&gt;
    /Users/jzhang/github/zeppelin&lt;br/&gt;
    ```&lt;/li&gt;
